<!-- order-refunded — money is on its way back (055 US5, FR-027).

     ⚠ IT SAYS "ON ITS WAY", NOT "REFUNDED", AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE MESSAGE. The provider
     accepting a refund is not the bank moving the money — that can take days and can still fail up to
     thirty days later. "Your refund is complete" would be a claim the platform cannot make, and it is
     the one claim that stops a shopper looking for money that never turned up.

     ⚠ IT PROMISES NO CREDIT LINE. A refund issued soon after payment often appears as a REVERSAL —
     the original charge simply vanishes from the statement and no separate credit ever shows up
     (research R2). A customer told to look for a credit will not find one, and will write to us about
     money that has already been returned.

     ⚠ THE TIMING SENTENCE IS THE PUBLISHED POLICY'S OWN, and the same one both customer surfaces
     render. Four places describing this would drift, and the one that drifts is whichever a developer
     edits without opening the legal document.

     ⚠ IT NAMES NO SHOP, NO PROVIDER AND NO FAILURE REASON. The catalogue gives this template no var
     to make those mistakes with — the same mechanism that makes a package count unrepresentable in
     order-delivered.

     ⚠ IT DOES NOT RESTATE THE RECEIPT. What was charged is a historical record sent at payment; this
     is a later event. Repeating the order total here would invite the reader to reconcile two
     documents produced at different moments. -->

<mjml lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <mj-head>
    <mj-include path="../generated/theme.mjml" />
    <mj-title>Your refund for order {{orderNumber}} is on its way</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>We&rsquo;ve sent the money back to your original payment method.</mj-preview>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body width="600px" background-color="#f5f5f5" css-class="e-bg-page">
    <mj-include path="../components/header.mjml" />

    <mj-section padding="0 32px 32px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text mj-class="h1" css-class="e-ink e-h1">
          Your refund is on its way
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text mj-class="muted" css-class="e-muted" padding="12px 0 0 0">
          We&rsquo;ve sent {{refundAmount}} back to the card or payment method you paid with for
          order {{orderNumber}}.
        </mj-text>

        <!-- ⚠ The honest timing, and the reversal warning. Both matter: without the first a shopper
             writes to us on day two, and without the second they write to us because they looked for
             a credit that will never appear. -->
        <mj-text mj-class="muted" css-class="e-muted" padding="16px 0 0 0">
          Refunds usually take a few business days, though when it appears depends on your bank. It
          may show as the original charge disappearing rather than as a separate credit.
        </mj-text>

        <!-- Both dark classes named so the label inverts with the fill — 038 shipped a receipt button
             that was invisible in dark mode because the class landed on the wrapping <td> while the
             colour sat on an inner element. -->
        <mj-button href="{{orderUrl}}" css-class="e-btn-bg e-btn-fg" align="left" padding="24px 0 0 0">
          View your order
        </mj-button>

        <mj-text mj-class="small" css-class="e-muted" padding="20px 0 0 0">
          Something not right? Reply to this email or write to {{effySupportEmail}} and we&rsquo;ll
          sort it out.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-include path="../components/footer.mjml" />
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
